# Launch the app

The Android project is `MaiMonthlyHoppinings/` (not the repo root). Package / application ID is `com.maimonthlyhoppinings`. There is no in-Cursor preview.

SDK on this machine: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Android\Sdk`. AVD: `Virtual_Device_-_API_35_Android_15`. Use Android Studio’s JBR as `JAVA_HOME` so Gradle is not run with a random system JDK.

```powershell
$sdk = "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Android\Sdk"
$env:ANDROID_HOME = $sdk
$env:ANDROID_SDK_ROOT = $sdk
$env:JAVA_HOME = "C:\Program Files\Android\Android Studio\jbr"
$env:Path = "$sdk\platform-tools;$sdk\emulator;$env:JAVA_HOME\bin;$env:Path"

# Start the emulator if adb devices is empty
emulator -avd Virtual_Device_-_API_35_Android_15
adb wait-for-device
# Wait until this prints 1
adb shell getprop sys.boot_completed

cd MaiMonthlyHoppinings
.\gradlew.bat :app:installDebug
adb shell am start -n com.maimonthlyhoppinings/.MainActivity
```

Do not run Gradle from the repo root. After a rename or `applicationId` change, uninstall the old package first; Android will not overwrite a different ID.

```powershell
adb uninstall com.howamidoing   # only if an old install is still present
```
